 worker owns argument\n  parsing, self-updates, queue processing, sleeping, and re-execing the latest\n  script before the next cycle.\n  §AR-do-work-loop\n  \n  Before self-update or queue processing, and again at the start of every\n  work-starting `forge_metadata.py` invocation, Forge validates the deterministic\n  host requirements for the tools, environment variables, filesystem and network\n  permissions, GitHub repository/project access, Docker, and agent authentication\n  its mode needs. Normal output prints only the check's start and outcome;\n  `--verbose` or a failure prints the complete report. A failed required check\n  exits before Forge claims or reviews anything; a `--review-pr` run is never\n  asked for a GraalVM.\n  §FS-forge-host-requirements\n  \n  The 25.0.x validation lane is pinned in `graalvm-versions.json`; update that\n  file when Forge should move to a newer 25.0.x release. The main and EA lanes are\n\n[Showing lines 240-502 of 3080 (50.0KB limit). Use offset=503 to continue.]"}], "details": {"truncation": {"content": "  ./stats/io.vertx/vertx-core/5.0.0/execution-metrics.json\n  ./stats/io.vertx/vertx-core/5.0.0/stats.json\n  ./stats/org.scala-sbt/test-interface/1.0/execution-metrics.json\n  ./stats/org.scala-sbt/test-interface/1.0/stats.json\n  ./metadata/org.apache.kafka/kafka-streams/index.json\n  ./metadata/org.apache.kafka/kafka-streams/3.5.1/reachability-metadata.json\n  ./metadata/org.apache.kafka/kafka-streams/3.6.0/reachability-metadata.json\n  ./stats/com.clickhouse/jdbc-v2/0.9.2/execution-metrics.json\n  ./stats/com.clickhouse/jdbc-v2/0.9.1/execution-metrics.json\n  ./stats/com.clickhouse/jdbc-v2/0.9.1/stats.json\n  ./stats/org.apache.groovy/groovy-test-junit5/4.0.24/execution-metrics.json\n  ./tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/dedicated-layer-test-exclusions.txt\n  ./tests/tck-build-logic/src/main/resources/shared-layered-test-exclusions.txt\n  ./tests/src/org.apache.kafka/kafka-streams/3.5.1/settings.gradle\n  ./tests/